From 909730a26a501f5003c670a48ce53bbe783e72ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yang Tsao <yang@fydeos.io>
Date: Fri, 8 May 2026 15:25:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] resolv_gold_test: build for primary arch only, not
 32-bit-only
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The original cc_test pinned compile_multilib: "32" as an MTS coverage
workaround (b/151392634). On a 64-bit-only ARM product (no
TARGET_2ND_ARCH), Soong produces no variant for the test, leaving
ALL_MODULES.resolv_gold_test.BUILT_INSTALLED empty. native_test_list.mk
then feeds that name into package-modules.mk's strict path, which
aborts ckati with "Unknown installed file for module 'resolv_gold_test'".

Switch to "first" so we always get a primary-arch build — 64-bit on
both our boards (fydroid-rt_arm64 and fydroid-rt_apple). AOSP 14 later
went to "both" with multilib suffixes, but that variant relies on
newer Soong putting the per-arch suffix into cc_test data: install
paths; in AOSP 11 the data still maps to a single
testcases/<name>/testdata/pb.zip and dual-build collides with itself.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I79a790a3a2790c8bc059e91696f95c806cfff2c9
---
 tests/Android.bp | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tests/Android.bp b/tests/Android.bp
index 2c65e45f..f913ed03 100644
--- a/tests/Android.bp
+++ b/tests/Android.bp
@@ -116,9 +116,13 @@ cc_test {
         "server_configurable_flags",
         "stats_proto",
     ],
-    // MTS test binary can't be built under compile_multilib = "both" and having test data.
-    // However, MTS coverage requires 32 bit test binary to run.
-    compile_multilib: "prefer32",
+    // Original "compile_multilib: 32" was an MTS coverage workaround
+    // (b/151392634); 13 stock uses "prefer32", AOSP 14 later relaxed it.
+    // We build the primary arch only — which gives us 64-bit installable
+    // test binaries on both 64-bit-only and dual-arch boards, while
+    // sidestepping the AOSP-11 Soong limitation where cc_test data: files
+    // don't take the multilib suffix and conflict if both variants build.
+    compile_multilib: "first",
 }
 
 cc_test {
-- 
2.43.0

